   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the town law and the public officers law, in relation to\nauthorizing the assistant court clerk and fire marshal of the town of\nHarrison, county of Westchester, to be nonresidents of such town",
    "basePrintNo": "S6426",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6426-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §23, Town L; amd §3, Pub Off L",
    "lawSection": "Town Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S6426\n\nSPONSOR: MAYER\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the town law and the public officers law, in relation to\nauthorizing the assistant court clerk and fire marshal of the town of\nHarrison, county of Westchester, to be nonresidents of such town\n\n \nPURPOSE OF BILL:\n\nTo waive the residency requirement for the assistant court clerk and\nfire marshal in the town of Harrison, county of Westchester\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends section 23 of the town law by adding subdivision 37 to\nallow the assistant court clerk and fire marshal of the town of Harrison\nto reside outside of the town as long as they reside within Westchester\nCounty.\n\nSection 2 amends section 3 of the public officers law by adding subdivi-\nsion 76 to allow the assistant court clerk and fire marshal of the town\nof Harrison to reside outside of the town as long as they reside within\nWestchester County.\n\nSection 3 sets the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation was requested by the town of Harrison. The bill allows\nthe town of Harrison to hire, for the positions of assistant court clerk\nand fire marshal, anyone who resides in the state of New York, so long\nas they reside in Westchester County. The town has sought to fill these\npositions for some time. This bill will expand the pool of eligible\ncandidates and will enable the town to hire the most qualified candi-\ndates for these positions.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
